WEBVTT

00:29.610 --> 00:31.870
If only it were me who had been crippled.

00:32.910 --> 00:35.240
Then you wouldn't have ended up like this.

01:52.140 --> 01:53.360
Damn cripple,

01:53.539 --> 01:54.800
are you blind?

01:56.120 --> 01:57.450
Do you even know who I am?

02:01.840 --> 02:03.170
Beat the hell out of him!

02:06.930 --> 02:07.980
You're glaring at me?

02:07.980 --> 02:08.520
Yeah.

02:15.020 --> 02:16.500
You want some too?

02:16.530 --> 02:17.600
Here, have some.

02:26.800 --> 02:28.870
I've got another little treat.

02:33.079 --> 02:33.810
Light him up!

02:39.560 --> 02:40.210
Run!

02:40.360 --> 02:41.540
Fun, right?

02:41.780 --> 02:42.500
Run!

02:45.150 --> 02:46.210
He's getting away.

02:57.920 --> 02:58.450
Let's go.

03:00.580 --> 03:01.510
Who the hell are you?

03:01.510 --> 03:03.070
Trying to play hero, huh?

03:03.880 --> 03:04.880
Stop right there!

03:15.310 --> 03:16.430
Need a hand?

03:18.970 --> 03:20.060
Are you a mute?

03:21.860 --> 03:23.410
I'm talking to you,

03:23.440 --> 03:24.770
damn cripple.

03:25.210 --> 03:26.680
I'm talking to you.

03:31.130 --> 03:32.910
Say something, you cripple!

03:38.970 --> 03:41.100
Rip his arm off!

06:26.190 --> 06:32.470
[Archives: The Nanyang Mystery]

06:32.980 --> 06:35.510
[Episode 17]

07:08.510 --> 07:09.470
Shrimpie...

07:12.120 --> 07:12.970
Shrimpie...

07:17.430 --> 07:18.330
Shrimpie...

07:24.150 --> 07:25.000
Shrimpie...

07:29.870 --> 07:30.600
Shrimpie...

07:48.930 --> 07:49.730
Young Master!

07:50.060 --> 07:51.560
How can you be out alone
with your legs like this?

07:51.560 --> 07:52.360
Young Master,

07:52.420 --> 07:53.880
how did you hurt your hand?

07:54.020 --> 07:55.620
Let me push your wheelchair.

07:58.860 --> 07:59.830
Get away from me.

08:03.500 --> 08:04.850
Don't come near me.

08:04.890 --> 08:06.980
B-But Young Master, your hand...

09:49.920 --> 09:50.850
What should I do?

09:51.810 --> 09:52.470
What...

09:54.480 --> 09:55.700
What should I do?

10:41.670 --> 10:42.470
Young Master?

10:43.080 --> 10:44.680
Young Master, you're awake.

10:46.030 --> 10:48.230
How did you get that injury on your hand?

10:52.360 --> 10:53.100
Yesterday,

10:53.220 --> 10:54.480
you came back injured,

10:54.500 --> 10:56.220
and your clothes were all soaked.

10:56.220 --> 10:57.270
If Young Master Hailou

10:57.270 --> 10:58.860
finds out you went out on your own,

10:58.860 --> 11:00.120
he'll be worried sick.

11:08.940 --> 11:11.330
Young Master, you're crippled.

11:11.350 --> 11:12.880
You should just stay in bed.

11:13.100 --> 11:14.620
You can't go wandering around on your own.

11:14.620 --> 11:15.310
Later,

11:15.370 --> 11:17.720
I should tell
Young Master Hailou about this.

11:17.720 --> 11:19.390
Otherwise, when he sees your injury,

11:19.390 --> 11:20.250
he'll blame me.

11:20.940 --> 11:23.320
Just stay in bed since you're crippled.

11:24.130 --> 11:26.730
You get hurt,
and then I have to take care of you.

11:53.600 --> 11:54.200
Shrimpie,

11:54.870 --> 11:55.930
what are you doing?

12:27.730 --> 12:28.280
I...

12:33.290 --> 12:34.350
What are you doing?

12:50.650 --> 12:51.780
It was all a dream...

13:24.590 --> 13:28.480
[Puguang Temple]

13:47.800 --> 13:54.630
[Almanac]

13:53.170 --> 13:54.620
Young sir,

13:55.250 --> 13:56.940
your aura is a bit stagnant.

13:57.100 --> 13:59.500
I'm afraid misfortune may be approaching.

14:00.840 --> 14:02.740
Why don't you let me read your fortune

14:02.740 --> 14:04.700
so we may find a way to avert it?

14:11.030 --> 14:12.090
You can't even see,

14:12.410 --> 14:14.030
yet you claim my aura is stagnant?

14:14.030 --> 14:15.690
That's a pretty lazy opening.

14:16.650 --> 14:18.720
Although I'm blind,

14:18.860 --> 14:20.500
my heart is not.

14:21.130 --> 14:21.860
Don't worry.

14:22.720 --> 14:25.240
I won't charge you a penny if I'm wrong.

14:29.100 --> 14:30.170
Young sir,

14:30.480 --> 14:34.150
has something been
weighing on your mind lately?

14:41.360 --> 14:42.290
In life,

14:43.270 --> 14:45.220
more often than not,
things don't turn out the way we'd hoped.

14:45.220 --> 14:47.100
But from what I can tell,

14:47.980 --> 14:49.390
your trouble

14:49.820 --> 14:51.600
comes from within,

14:51.670 --> 14:53.270
not from anything external.

14:53.840 --> 14:55.960
And this has never

14:55.960 --> 14:58.510
happened to you before.

15:00.240 --> 15:01.500
Am I right?

15:23.240 --> 15:25.930
Have you long been afflicted with illness

15:25.980 --> 15:28.440
and only recently recovered?

15:30.770 --> 15:33.220
Then can you divine
what it is that has been troubling me?

15:33.220 --> 15:34.440
As the saying goes,

15:34.670 --> 15:37.500
wisdom is neither imparted lightly
nor sold cheaply.

15:37.500 --> 15:40.580
Young sir, if you're willing to
make a small offering,

15:41.150 --> 15:43.150
though I'm no immortal,

15:43.240 --> 15:44.670
perhaps I can try

15:44.720 --> 15:47.000
to unravel what troubles your heart.

15:56.340 --> 15:58.270
Since recovering from my illness,

15:58.320 --> 16:01.050
I've been haunted over and over again
by a thought

16:02.360 --> 16:03.370
I cannot explain.

16:07.010 --> 16:08.650
I don't want to act on it,

16:10.650 --> 16:12.150
but it disturbs my mind,

16:13.080 --> 16:14.410
and I can't suppress it.

16:18.460 --> 16:20.060
I don't know if, at this rate,

16:21.890 --> 16:23.550
it'll eventually consume me.

16:29.120 --> 16:31.380
And I don't know whether I can destroy it.

16:33.940 --> 16:35.140
From my perspective,

16:35.220 --> 16:37.630
you should not fight it.

16:37.790 --> 16:41.270
Follow your heart
and see that thought through.

16:41.770 --> 16:44.890
When you do,
the answer will reveal itself.

16:51.130 --> 16:52.370
That's your advice?

16:53.320 --> 16:55.550
Young man, you must know

16:55.770 --> 16:57.530
that fate cannot be defied.

16:57.550 --> 16:58.960
No matter how hard you struggle,

16:58.960 --> 17:00.960
you will eventually walk

17:00.960 --> 17:03.290
the path you are meant to walk.

17:16.420 --> 17:19.480
You said you wouldn't charge
if your reading was wrong.

17:20.200 --> 17:21.460
Well, your reading...

17:25.380 --> 17:25.960
is wrong.

18:17.850 --> 18:18.450
Shrimpie.

18:19.280 --> 18:20.860
Look at the fish I cured.

18:21.330 --> 18:21.790
Come on.

18:23.440 --> 18:24.570
Give me some praise.

18:28.220 --> 18:29.750
What happened to your hand?

18:30.750 --> 18:32.480
Had too much to drink last night

18:33.110 --> 18:34.200
and took a spill.

18:34.530 --> 18:35.200
Let me see.

18:37.400 --> 18:38.200
Zhang Hailou.

18:40.380 --> 18:40.880
I...

18:49.740 --> 18:51.070
Come take a walk with me.

19:00.670 --> 19:03.250
[Gentle Breeze and Harmonious Air]

19:03.250 --> 19:07.010
[Qiyuan Tea Shop]

19:22.420 --> 19:23.020
Shrimpie,

19:23.500 --> 19:24.830
do you still remember
when we were in Nanyang,

19:24.830 --> 19:26.420
and I really craved pork trotter noodles?

19:26.420 --> 19:28.220
We were too broke to afford them.

19:28.640 --> 19:30.790
And you told me we'd eat our fill
once we got back to Xiacheng.

19:30.790 --> 19:31.400
Look.

19:33.640 --> 19:35.110
Haihua Grocery Store.

19:36.440 --> 19:39.010
Doesn't that sound exactly like
one of our family's businesses?

19:39.010 --> 19:39.870
It's right across the street.

19:39.870 --> 19:42.730
How about we buy this shop
and turn it into a pig farm?

19:44.440 --> 19:45.790
Can't we afford pork trotter noodles

19:45.790 --> 19:47.110
anytime we want now?

19:47.680 --> 19:49.550
Wouldn't it be a waste
to keep buying them?

19:49.550 --> 19:51.380
Besides, our mentor is so reckless.

19:51.380 --> 19:51.960
Who knows

19:51.980 --> 19:53.590
when she'll blow through
her entire nest egg?

19:53.590 --> 19:55.450
We've got to plan ahead, don't we?

19:56.540 --> 19:57.550
Three of us...

19:57.850 --> 20:00.050
T-Thirty pigs should be enough, right?

20:03.740 --> 20:05.600
Why have you been so quiet lately?

20:05.600 --> 20:06.580
Say something.

20:09.850 --> 20:10.650
Zhang Hailou.

20:18.750 --> 20:19.680
Actually, lately I've...

20:19.680 --> 20:22.720
-Chief!
-Chief!

20:21.570 --> 20:22.900
[Haihua Grocery Store]

20:22.720 --> 20:24.070
Chief, we're here!

20:24.070 --> 20:25.130
You're here, kids.

20:27.350 --> 20:28.080
Stand still.

20:31.160 --> 20:33.010
They're just a bunch of kids
from the neighborhood.

20:33.010 --> 20:34.180
They practically idolize me.

20:34.180 --> 20:35.350
Pick out some good ones,

20:35.350 --> 20:38.350
and we can train them
as new recruits for our Archives.

20:40.730 --> 20:41.790
Alright, speak up—

20:42.110 --> 20:43.350
why did you come to me?

20:43.870 --> 20:46.790
Chief, he has a grievance to report!

20:47.980 --> 20:48.710
A grievance?

20:49.680 --> 20:50.480
Let's hear it.

20:52.570 --> 20:53.010
He...

20:55.140 --> 20:56.010
He's a bad guy!

20:57.140 --> 20:58.470
He wanted to kill my cat!

21:04.790 --> 21:06.540
Do you know what you're saying?

21:07.550 --> 21:08.550
Let me ask you all—

21:09.010 --> 21:10.480
who is the greatest in Xiacheng?

21:10.480 --> 21:11.960
You, Chief.

21:12.090 --> 21:13.070
I'm the Chief,

21:13.590 --> 21:14.980
and he's the Second Chief.

21:14.980 --> 21:16.910
Could the Second Chief be a bad guy?

21:16.980 --> 21:18.780
Let's see who dares slander him.

21:20.980 --> 21:22.030
Is it you? Is it you?

21:22.030 --> 21:22.740
Is it you?

21:24.940 --> 21:26.610
Yuanbao isn't lying.

21:26.640 --> 21:27.740
What he says is true.

21:27.740 --> 21:28.640
He's telling the truth.

21:28.640 --> 21:29.440
Believe us.

21:29.500 --> 21:30.860
Listen to us.

21:30.980 --> 21:32.310
Yuanbao is telling the truth.

21:32.310 --> 21:33.550
Yuanbao isn't lying.

21:33.610 --> 21:34.920
He's not lying.

21:34.920 --> 21:36.440
We're telling the truth.

21:36.460 --> 21:38.120
Yuanbao is telling the truth.

21:38.420 --> 21:39.660
Yuanbao isn't lying.

21:39.660 --> 21:41.210
Believe us! Believe us!

21:41.240 --> 21:42.770
We're not lying.

21:42.770 --> 21:44.000
What he says is true.

21:44.070 --> 21:45.420
Yuanbao...
Yuanbao is really telling the truth.

21:45.420 --> 21:46.660
Alright, alright, enough.

21:46.660 --> 21:49.310
Looks like this is
another mystery with no clues.

21:49.310 --> 21:52.700
How about this? After I'm properly dressed
in my official robes,

21:52.700 --> 21:54.360
I'll settle this case for you.

21:54.680 --> 21:55.210
Let's go.

21:55.570 --> 21:56.050
Go in.

21:57.160 --> 21:58.070
Chief!

21:58.070 --> 21:59.220
Wait for me!

21:59.290 --> 21:59.980
Chief!

21:59.980 --> 22:01.250
You wanted to kill my cat!

22:01.250 --> 22:02.180
You're a bad guy!

22:02.250 --> 22:03.250
You're a bad guy!

22:53.200 --> 22:55.380
Help! Help!

22:56.500 --> 22:58.330
Help! Help!

22:59.250 --> 23:00.310
Help!

23:00.380 --> 23:01.430
Help!

23:01.920 --> 23:04.260
-Wait for me!
-Wait for us!

23:04.380 --> 23:05.530
Chief!

23:05.680 --> 23:06.920
Help!

23:07.680 --> 23:08.140
Help!

23:08.140 --> 23:09.740
-I'll go check it out.
-Help!

23:11.250 --> 23:12.310
Yuanbao!

23:12.330 --> 23:13.050
Yuanbao!

23:13.050 --> 23:13.580
Yuanbao!

23:13.610 --> 23:14.210
Shrimpie.

23:15.160 --> 23:15.960
What was that?

23:19.140 --> 23:20.540
Why are you hiding there?

23:23.510 --> 23:24.530
Bring him back to me.

23:24.530 --> 23:25.050
Okay.

23:35.610 --> 23:36.210
Shrimpie.

23:36.480 --> 23:37.680
Stop playing around.

23:38.960 --> 23:40.560
You just play around all day.

23:41.070 --> 23:42.070
That's all you do.

23:42.310 --> 23:44.510
Can playing around solve our problems?

23:48.210 --> 23:50.200
Fine, I won't play with them anymore.

23:50.200 --> 23:51.860
You've got blood on your nose.

23:52.850 --> 23:53.550
I'm fine.

23:57.510 --> 23:58.570
Fine? You're fine?

23:58.810 --> 23:59.940
You call this fine?

23:59.970 --> 24:01.500
I said I'm fine, so I am fine.

24:07.240 --> 24:08.750
-Chief!
-Chief!

24:08.750 --> 24:09.440
Chief!

24:09.440 --> 24:10.980
Yuanbao is crying.

24:10.980 --> 24:12.070
Yuanbao is crying.

24:12.070 --> 24:12.510
Alright.

24:12.510 --> 24:15.180
The Chiefs have
serious matters to discuss.

24:16.250 --> 24:17.550
You guys l-leave first.

24:17.550 --> 24:18.800
Stop playing!

24:19.610 --> 24:21.270
I said, stop playing around with them!

24:21.270 --> 24:22.830
Do you even understand?

24:30.250 --> 24:31.420
Avenge Yuanbao!

24:31.550 --> 24:32.920
Avenge Yuanbao!

24:32.980 --> 24:34.250
Avenge Yuanbao!

24:34.310 --> 24:35.160
Avenge Yuanbao!

24:35.160 --> 24:36.310
Get justice for Yuanbao!

24:36.310 --> 24:37.240
Chief!

24:37.290 --> 24:38.830
Avenge Yuanbao!

24:38.900 --> 24:39.510
Stand up for Yuanbao!

24:39.510 --> 24:40.350
Listen up,

24:41.310 --> 24:42.480
when the Chiefs

24:42.510 --> 24:43.560
are talking business,

24:43.560 --> 24:45.400
don't be chirping away like this,
understand?

24:45.400 --> 24:46.640
Avenge Yuanbao!

24:46.900 --> 24:48.220
Avenge Yuanbao!

24:48.270 --> 24:49.620
Avenge Yuanbao!

24:49.980 --> 24:51.530
Avenge Yuanbao!

24:52.590 --> 24:54.050
Avenge Yuanbao!

24:56.070 --> 24:57.330
Avenge Yuanbao!

24:57.420 --> 24:58.850
Avenge Yuanbao!

24:58.850 --> 25:00.790
Avenge Yuanbao!

25:05.350 --> 25:06.740
Avenge Yuanbao!

25:17.900 --> 25:19.830
The Second Chief is getting angry!

25:21.280 --> 25:22.570
Enough. Leave now.

25:22.670 --> 25:26.000
Otherwise, even I won't be able to
protect you, understand?

25:27.790 --> 25:30.360
Chief, avenge Yuanbao!

25:30.590 --> 25:33.010
Chief, avenge Yuanbao!

25:33.790 --> 25:34.990
What's all the noise?

25:41.770 --> 25:42.240
Mentor.

25:42.590 --> 25:43.350
Meeting.

25:47.050 --> 25:49.740
Chief, please believe us!

25:49.810 --> 25:51.100
Chief,

25:51.380 --> 25:53.800
didn't you promise to protect us?

25:53.850 --> 25:55.020
Chief.

25:55.550 --> 25:57.660
Chief, avenge Yuanbao!

25:57.770 --> 25:59.610
Chief, believe us!

25:59.750 --> 26:01.720
There are only three of us left
in the Southern Archives.

26:01.720 --> 26:02.740
And you both know

26:02.740 --> 26:03.790
who our enemy is.

26:04.070 --> 26:04.790
A few days ago,

26:04.790 --> 26:06.720
the Mo faction warlords
withdrew from Xiacheng.

26:06.650 --> 26:08.630
[Xiacheng News]

26:06.900 --> 26:09.170
The consulate is negotiating with
the government.

26:09.170 --> 26:11.290
Due to the deaths of Warner and his group,

26:11.290 --> 26:13.580
[Should the Mo faction
bear responsibility?]

26:11.550 --> 26:13.970
they're holding
the Beilian warlord Mo Yungao accountable—

26:13.970 --> 26:17.030
the man responsible for
the slaughter of the Archives.

26:17.220 --> 26:18.310
The situation is volatile now.

26:18.310 --> 26:20.160
The government's word isn't worth a damn.

26:20.160 --> 26:21.310
What's the use of
demanding accountability?

26:21.310 --> 26:22.190
Where is he?

26:24.010 --> 26:25.070
Going after him...

26:26.960 --> 26:27.810
won't be easy.

26:29.770 --> 26:31.400
That was before his promotion.

26:31.400 --> 26:32.530
In just a few months,

26:32.550 --> 26:34.050
he rose to division commander

26:34.050 --> 26:36.030
and quickly took control
of all of Beilian.

26:36.030 --> 26:37.610
He's not like ordinary warlords.

26:37.610 --> 26:39.610
Officially, he answers to
the coalition military government,

26:39.610 --> 26:40.470
but in reality,

26:40.920 --> 26:42.320
he rules independently.

26:43.200 --> 26:44.750
His relationship with the government
is complicated.

26:44.750 --> 26:46.350
So the government prefers to

26:46.550 --> 26:47.500
placate him

26:48.330 --> 26:50.260
rather than provoke him directly.

26:50.440 --> 26:54.000
On top of that, he has many skilled fighters
around him at all times.

26:54.000 --> 26:55.440
You won't be able to get close to him.

26:55.440 --> 26:56.360
I get it.

26:56.660 --> 26:58.400
Mo Yungao is basically a local kingpin

26:58.400 --> 26:59.660
with enormous power.

27:00.440 --> 27:01.050
So what?

27:01.660 --> 27:03.680
Does he have soldiers guarding him

27:03.770 --> 27:05.830
even when he eats, sleeps, and shits?

27:06.920 --> 27:07.920
To take him out,

27:08.160 --> 27:09.850
we first need to
figure out his whereabouts

27:09.850 --> 27:11.140
and his plan.

27:11.980 --> 27:12.550
Haixia.

27:14.750 --> 27:16.810
This is a secret letter I memorized

27:16.940 --> 27:18.940
while I was being hunted on the ship.

27:24.030 --> 27:24.590
Hold on.

27:25.480 --> 27:27.350
When did you two
have a meeting on that ship

27:27.350 --> 27:28.460
and leave me out of it?

27:28.460 --> 27:29.850
It wasn't on the ship.

27:30.220 --> 27:31.620
It was before you woke up.

27:32.200 --> 27:34.600
He told me everything he discovered there.

27:43.200 --> 27:45.680
"If the Pitcher Plant Project succeeds,

27:43.270 --> 27:47.160
[Nanling] [Chuhan]
[Guangchuan] [Changxiang]

27:45.920 --> 27:48.380
and all Archives personnel are eliminated,

27:49.000 --> 27:51.200
proceed immediately to the next phase.

27:52.200 --> 27:52.860
This is

27:54.090 --> 27:55.530
20 years of my life's work.

27:55.530 --> 27:56.530
It must not fail."

27:57.850 --> 27:58.710
So Mo Yungao

27:58.740 --> 28:00.470
will keep stirring up trouble?

28:00.510 --> 28:01.530
My deduction is

28:01.660 --> 28:03.790
that Mo Yungao has encrypted his plan,

28:04.010 --> 28:06.540
and these four illustrations
are the cipher.

28:06.640 --> 28:08.270
The codebook is an ancient prophecy text

28:08.270 --> 28:09.930
called "Hongmeng Prophecy."

28:11.440 --> 28:13.890
I knew the Archives had the original copy,

28:15.700 --> 28:18.100
and I was the only one
who could retrieve it.

28:20.180 --> 28:22.110
That's why I couldn't die back then

28:22.850 --> 28:23.770
and chose to...

28:25.460 --> 28:26.260
fake my death.

28:37.220 --> 28:38.880
But I was also taking a gamble,

28:39.610 --> 28:41.670
betting on whether you could save me.

28:47.740 --> 28:49.340
Fortunately, I won that bet.

28:57.310 --> 28:59.220
So why are you the only one
who can get that book?

28:59.220 --> 29:01.160
Some of the Archives'
most valuable evidence

29:01.160 --> 29:04.250
is stored inside mechanical lockboxes.

29:04.350 --> 29:06.500
If someone opens one incorrectly
or tries to force it open,

29:06.500 --> 29:07.350
the acid sealed inside

29:07.350 --> 29:09.270
will dissolve all the evidence

29:09.420 --> 29:10.900
to prevent it from leaking.

29:10.900 --> 29:12.230
In the entire Archives,

29:12.460 --> 29:13.450
he's the only one

29:14.050 --> 29:15.450
capable of opening them.

30:23.500 --> 30:24.630
Can you decipher it?

30:30.390 --> 30:31.530
[Nanling] [Chuhan]
[Guangchuan] [Changxiang]

30:42.170 --> 30:44.460
[Moon]

30:52.710 --> 30:53.550
[Ancient Capital] [Nanling]

30:53.570 --> 30:54.340
[Nine Curves] [Dragon's Roar]

30:54.370 --> 30:55.210
[Hundred Cranes] [Lonely Moon]

30:55.250 --> 30:56.810
[Nanling] [Chuhan]
[Guangchuan] [Changxiang]

31:02.960 --> 31:05.190
[Nanling]

31:05.540 --> 31:08.620
[Detailed Coastal Topography Map]

31:05.660 --> 31:06.400
Nanling,

31:06.530 --> 31:07.380
Chuhan,

31:07.570 --> 31:08.300
Guangchuan,

31:08.310 --> 31:09.200
Changxiang...

31:31.440 --> 31:32.310
These are the villages

31:32.310 --> 31:35.840
where the Twilight Grass poison outbreak
occurred in Nanyang.

31:40.070 --> 31:41.750
Connected in chronological order...

31:41.580 --> 31:45.840
[Xucheng] [Jilanna]

31:46.310 --> 31:47.170
they lead here.

31:53.170 --> 31:55.220
[Nanling] [Chuhan]
[Guangchuan] [Changxiang]

31:54.500 --> 31:55.550
So the Twilight Grass incident in Nanyang

31:55.240 --> 31:56.250
[Xucheng] [Jilanna]

31:55.550 --> 31:56.810
was merely a trial run.

31:58.350 --> 31:59.060
Looks like

31:59.180 --> 32:01.630
he's ready to do it for real
on the mainland now.

32:01.630 --> 32:02.940
We must stop him.

32:05.590 --> 32:06.290
It's just that...

32:06.290 --> 32:08.790
We have no way to predict
when he'll make his move.

32:08.790 --> 32:11.030
The Mo faction has suffered
such heavy losses,

32:11.030 --> 32:12.170
so they probably can't act anytime soon.

32:12.170 --> 32:13.350
Facing a well-armed army

32:13.350 --> 32:15.240
of this size...

32:17.160 --> 32:20.420
the three of us alone
have little chance of wiping them out.

32:24.920 --> 32:25.510
Mentor,

32:26.680 --> 32:28.480
our Zhang family is so powerful.

32:28.570 --> 32:30.640
Now that our Southern Archives
has been taken out,

32:30.640 --> 32:31.920
won't the Western, Northern,

32:31.920 --> 32:33.200
and Eastern branches

32:33.310 --> 32:35.110
send reinforcements to help us?

32:35.420 --> 32:36.680
We can't count on them.

32:45.610 --> 32:46.670
They're no help,

32:47.010 --> 32:48.210
but we still have you.

32:49.000 --> 32:51.270
Mentor, what are your thoughts now?

32:51.700 --> 32:53.400
To bring down Mo Yungao

32:53.480 --> 32:55.540
and rebuild the Archives, of course.

33:01.160 --> 33:01.750
Mentor,

33:02.420 --> 33:04.480
you've already got a plan, don't you?

33:08.300 --> 33:10.880
We'll go to Changxiang
to seek help from someone.

33:10.880 --> 33:12.720
He should know about Mo Yungao.

33:13.510 --> 33:16.050
He may be able to help us track him down

33:16.180 --> 33:17.640
and lend us some manpower.

33:18.480 --> 33:18.980
Who?

33:19.570 --> 33:20.700
We're short on time.

33:20.790 --> 33:22.120
I'll explain on the way.

33:22.720 --> 33:23.680
Zhang Haixia,

33:23.830 --> 33:25.140
you won't be traveling with us.

33:25.140 --> 33:26.270
You'll leave first.

33:26.700 --> 33:27.380
Mentor,

33:27.920 --> 33:29.180
I'll go with Shrimpie.

33:29.420 --> 33:31.150
I can take care of him on the way.

33:31.240 --> 33:33.870
This trip to Changxiang is very dangerous.

33:34.070 --> 33:35.360
I need you with me.

33:35.900 --> 33:37.290
I have other plans for him.

33:37.290 --> 33:39.350
I'll have someone I trust escort you.

33:44.350 --> 33:46.750
-No matter how reliable they are...
-Okay.

33:47.350 --> 33:48.330
In that case,

33:49.200 --> 33:50.400
tomorrow morning...

33:55.440 --> 33:56.970
we will set off separately.

34:27.030 --> 34:28.230
You can feel them now?

34:29.590 --> 34:31.590
That means you're recovering well.

34:32.110 --> 34:33.370
It's been three years.

34:33.500 --> 34:34.429
How does it feel?

34:37.570 --> 34:38.699
Not much, I suppose.

34:40.510 --> 34:42.909
Isn't there still a chance
I'll get better?

34:45.330 --> 34:47.460
You've been this way since childhood,

34:47.530 --> 34:49.670
always keeping
everything bottled up inside.

34:49.670 --> 34:52.670
You need to think about yourself too,
not just others.

34:52.730 --> 34:53.190
Come on.

34:53.900 --> 34:55.370
I was raised by you.

34:57.320 --> 34:58.450
Aren't you the same?

34:59.550 --> 35:00.230
No.

35:05.200 --> 35:07.460
Is it because I don't have much time left?

35:12.130 --> 35:14.250
Mentor, you told me

35:15.480 --> 35:17.580
that the fake-death drug
is actually a poison—

35:17.580 --> 35:19.040
that it only delays death,

35:19.530 --> 35:21.590
and in the end, the person still dies.

35:25.280 --> 35:26.300
How will I die?

35:33.680 --> 35:36.410
The fake-death drug
actually comes in two doses.

35:37.860 --> 35:40.520
The first dose is the poison
you took on the ship,

35:40.920 --> 35:43.050
which put you into a death-like state.

35:45.470 --> 35:47.270
The second dose is also a poison—

35:47.650 --> 35:49.310
fighting poison with poison.

35:49.800 --> 35:51.420
It can wake you up,

35:52.010 --> 35:53.780
but it also affects the brain.

35:54.780 --> 35:57.710
I originally didn't want to
give you the second dose.

36:01.170 --> 36:03.430
The first agent who ever used that poison

36:04.880 --> 36:06.480
began losing control

36:07.440 --> 36:09.100
not long after being revived.

36:09.670 --> 36:12.270
He became extremely
agitated and aggressive.

36:12.480 --> 36:14.030
During an assignment,

36:14.150 --> 36:16.010
he slaughtered an entire village

36:17.030 --> 36:18.230
without any warning,

36:19.260 --> 36:20.860
and no one could control him.

36:22.260 --> 36:23.000
So...

36:26.050 --> 36:27.980
everyone who has ever used the drug

36:28.640 --> 36:30.970
has ultimately been killed by my own hand.

36:37.380 --> 36:38.130
Mentor...

36:42.460 --> 36:43.780
Will you kill me too?
